          "type": "tab_content",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How Large Is The Dog Vacuum Dustbin?",
            "text": "<p>Oneisall Dog Vacuum offers large dustbin capacities ranging from 1.5 to 3l. </p><p>A small dog (like a Shih Tzu or Chihuahua) may produce 0.5 to 1 L of loose hair after a full grooming session.</p><p>Medium and large breeds with thick coats (like Golden Retrievers or German Shepherds) can produce 1 to 3 L of hair</p><p>The large bin is suited for grooming multiple pets or a larger pet.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_content_c6HcW7": {
          "type": "tab_content",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is The Pet Water Fountain Easy To Assemble?",
            "text": "<p>Yes. Most pet water fountains are easy to assemble and designed to be user-friendly. The process usually involves a few simple steps and can be done in minutes. </p><p>Here's a basic outline of what to expect:</p><ul><li>Put filter cotton into the filter box</li><li>Assemble the pump</li><li>Fill the tank with water</li><li>Put on the cover drinking tray and insert the faucet</li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "tab_content_Rpa4Mk": {
          "type": "tab_content",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I Use A Cat Water Fountain For Both Cats And Dogs?",
            "text": "<p>Yes, many cat water fountains are designed to accommodate both cats and dogs. Choose a cat water fountain for your pet's size and breed. Larger dogs may require a pet drinking fountain with a higher water capacity.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_content_3rqzKM": {
          "type": "tab_content",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What Should I Look For When Choosing An Automatic Feeder For Cats?",
            "text": "<p>To set the timer on an automatic feeder for cats, follow these 5 steps:</p><p>1. Open the feeder’s control panel or app (depending on the model).</p><p>2. Set the desired meal times using the built-in timer or mobile app.</p><p>3. Adjust the portion size for each meal.</p><p>4. Ensure the automatic feeder for cats is loaded with food, then activate the timer.</p><p>5. Check the user manual for specific instructions, as each model may vary slightly.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
